\begin{abstract}
This reproducible teaching demonstration executes a constrained numerical model, registers its verified result, and renders a report from that single result source. The computed optimum is \texttt{{{OPTIMUM}}}, while the independent feasibility audit is recorded in the attached validation report. Keywords: reproducibility; validation gate; artifact registry.
\end{abstract}
\tableofcontents\newpage
\section{Problem and model}
The objective is to minimise $(x-2)^2$ subject to $0\le x\le3$. The solver result is sourced only from the verified JSON artifact; solver tolerance is not described as model error.
\section{Result and validation}
The calculated optimum is $x={{{OPTIMUM}}}$ and the residual is ${{{RESIDUAL}}}$. Figure~\ref{fig:objective} shows the full response and a registered source artifact. The validation gate confirms the bound and numerical residual.
\begin{figure}[h]
\centering\includegraphics[width=0.72\linewidth]{objective.png}
\caption{Objective response and the verified minimizer.}\label{fig:objective}
\end{figure}
\section{Limitations}
This is a teaching-scale model, not a competition submission. Visual clipping, font substitution, and caption layout remain explicitly marked for manual review by PDF preflight.
